TIP:  To play the intro, first form (G7) using your index finger on the 1st string/1st fret of the <f#>.  Now add your pinky to cover the 1st string/3rd fret <g>.  So now you have both the (G) and the (G7) chords at the ready, playing (G7) by just lifting off the pinky.  So start the intro with two strums of (G), one more and then lift off the pinky to play the (G7), move your pinky up one string to the 2nd string/3rd fret for the (G7addD), and then play a normal (G) aiming for the 2nd and 3rd strings.  If you're careful to avoid the 1st string you can even keep the (G7) form after lifting off the (G7addD). 


